module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.CechGermBaseChangeProof
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.RingBaseChangeAugmentation

/-!
# Stacks 099D, condition (d): the Čech identification at an arbitrary pair

[Stacks, Tag 099D], condition (d), asks that the complex `K(A, I)` of step 2 be identified in
`D(A)` with the extended alternating Čech complex on *any* finite generating family of `I`,
compatibly with the augmentations. For a *presented* pair that is the datum's own field
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum.exists_cech_iso`; **this file proves it for every pair**
`(A, I)` with `I` finitely generated, which is `Stacks.PairSite.ColimitCechIso`.

## The argument

Let `f₁, …, f_r` generate `I`. By `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_lift_span` there is an
object `X` of the index category of step 2 whose ideal is generated by *lifts* `g₁, …, g_r` of the
`f i`; write `R = X.pair.ring` and `φ : R → A` for its structure map, so that `f = φ ∘ g`. Two
base-change comparisons along `φ` are then available, and both are isomorphisms:

* at the Čech complexes, `C^•(g; R) ⊗^L_R A ⟶ C^•(f; A)`, by
  `Stacks.CechRingBaseChange.isIso_derivedBaseChange_extendedComplexMap`;
* at the germ map, `𝒦•(X.pair) ⊗^L_R A ⟶ K(A, I)`, by `Stacks.PairSite.germBaseChange`.

The datum's own condition (d) at `X.pair` supplies an isomorphism `C^•(g; R) ≅ 𝒦•(X.pair)` in
`D(R)`; base-changing it along `φ` and composing with the two comparisons gives the isomorphism
`C^•(f; A) ≅ K(A, I)` of `D(A)` that condition (d) asks for.

The augmentations match because *condition (a) holds for both models at `φ`*, on the nose: for
the Čech model it is `Stacks.CechRingBaseChange.extendedComplexMap_augmentation` and for the
colimit it is `Stacks.PairSite.germComplexMap_augmentation`. Both squares exhibit the composite
of the base-change comparison with the localized augmentation as `φ`'s own base-change comparison
`A ⊗^L_R R[0] ⟶ A[0]` preceded by the image of the augmentation upstairs — see
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares`, which is where that calculation is
carried out once, with the complexes as variables.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares` — the transport of an
  augmentation-compatible isomorphism along two invertible base-change comparisons whose
  augmentation squares commute on the nose.
* `Stacks.PairSite.colimitCechIso` — **condition (d) of the tag for the colimit complex of step
  2, at every pair**, with no hypothesis beyond the datum.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks 099D]` attribute is attached: the tag asks for an unconditional
`Nonempty Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData`, and what is proved here is one condition of
it. With this file and `Stacks.PairSite.colimitBaseChange`, every field of that structure follows
from a `Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum` through
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData_of_presented`; the datum itself is
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_presentedCechDatum`, and the assembled term, which carries the attribute,
is `Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_functorialCechData`.

`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares` takes its four complexes as explicit
arguments and `Stacks.LocalCohomology.comp_eq_of_comp_iso_inv` takes its objects as variables.
The reason is the one recorded in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/CechGermBaseChange.lean`: the
comparison maps of derived extension of scalars have types spelled with
`CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars.extensionOfScalarsComplexGeneral`, a `def` built by
tactics, so `rw` and `simp` fail on goals mentioning them while `exact` — which checks at default
transparency — succeeds. Stating the step with variable objects does the rewriting in the
elaborator instead. The same holds for the two spellings
`CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ` and `(ModuleCat.restrictScalars φ).mapHomologicalComplex _` of
restriction of scalars on complexes, which the two models use respectively.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

open CochainComplex.DerivedExtensionScalars

/-- **Cancel an isomorphism off the right of a factorization.** Stated with the objects as
variables on purpose: it is applied to the augmentation identity of
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum.exists_cech_iso`, whose right-hand side is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentationHom`, a `def` that `rw` will not unfold. -/
theorem comp_eq_of_comp_iso_inv {C : Type*} [Category C] {W X Y Z : C} (p : W ⟶ X) (q : X ⟶ Y)
    (ι : Z ≅ Y) (m : W ⟶ Y) (h : p ≫ q ≫ ι.inv = m ≫ ι.inv) : p ≫ q = m := by
  simpa only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]
    using congrArg (fun t => t ≫ ι.hom) h

section Squares

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]

/-- **Transporting an augmentation-compatible isomorphism along two base changes.** Let
`φ : A → B` be a ring map, let `Kc` and `Ks` be complexes of `A`-modules augmented onto `A`, let
`Lc` and `Ls` be complexes of `B`-modules augmented onto `B`, and let `uc : Kc → Lc` and
`us : Ks → Ls` be maps of complexes of `A`-modules commuting with the augmentations and `φ` on
the nose — condition (a) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for two models. Assume both base-change
comparisons `Kc ⊗^L_A B → Lc` and `Ks ⊗^L_A B → Ls` are isomorphisms — condition (c) for the two
models — and that `Kc` and `Ks` are isomorphic in `D(A)` over their augmentations. Then `Lc` and
`Ls` are isomorphic in `D(B)` over theirs.

This is the step that carries condition (d) from a presented pair to the pair below it: `Kc` is
the Čech complex upstairs, `Ks` the complex of the datum there, and `Lc`, `Ls` their
counterparts downstairs. Both augmentation squares are turned by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_right` and
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedBaseChange_comp_left` into the *same* comparison
`B ⊗^L_A A[0] ⟶ B[0]`, preceded by the image of the augmentation upstairs, so the two models
are compared through a single morphism. -/
theorem exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares (φ : A →+* B)
    (Kc Ks : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ) (Lc Ls : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ)
    (uc : Kc ⟶ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj Lc)
    (us : Ks ⟶ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj Ls)
    (ac : Kc ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A))
    (asc : Ks ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A))
    (bc : Lc ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of B B))
    (bs : Ls ⟶ (CochainComplex.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of B B))
    (hc : uc ≫ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map bc = ac ≫ singleRingHom φ)
    (hs : us ≫ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map bs = asc ≫ singleRingHom φ)
    (hic : IsIso (derivedBaseChange φ uc)) (his : IsIso (derivedBaseChange φ us))
    (ε : DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kc ≅ DerivedCategory.Q.obj Ks)
    (hε : ε.hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map asc = DerivedCategory.Q.map ac) :
    ∃ e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj Lc ≅ DerivedCategory.Q.obj Ls,
      e.hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map bs = DerivedCategory.Q.map bc := by
  have := hic
  have := his
  have key {K : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ} {L : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} B) ℤ}
      (u : K ⟶ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).obj L) (a : K ⟶ _) (b : L ⟶ _)
      (h : u ≫ (CochainComplex.restrictScalars φ).map b = a ≫ singleRingHom φ) :
      derivedBaseChange φ u ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map b =
        (derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} φ).functor.map (DerivedCategory.Q.map a) ≫
          derivedBaseChange φ (singleRingHom φ) := by
    rw [← derivedBaseChange_comp_right φ u b, h, derivedBaseChange_comp_left]
  refine ⟨(asIso (derivedBaseChange φ uc)).symm ≪≫
    (derivedExtensionScalarsGeneral.{u, u, u} φ).functor.mapIso ε ≪≫
      asIso (derivedBaseChange φ us), ?_⟩
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, asIso_hom, asIso_inv, Functor.mapIso_hom,
    Category.assoc]
  rw [key us asc bs hs, ← Functor.map_comp_assoc, hε, ← key uc ac bc hc, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

end Squares

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

namespace Stacks.PairSite

open PairOver Stacks.CechRingBaseChange

/-- **Condition (d) of [Stacks, Tag 099D] for the colimit complex of step 2, at every pair.** For
a ring `A`, a finitely generated ideal `I` and *any* finite family `f₁, …, f_r` generating `I`,
there is an isomorphism in `D(A)` from the extended alternating Čech complex on `f₁, …, f_r` to
the colimit complex `K(A, I)` of step 2, carrying the augmentation of the former onto that of the
latter.

Choose, by `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_lift_span`, an object `X` of the index
category whose ideal is generated by lifts `g₁, …, g_r` of the `f i` along its structure map
`φ : R → A`, so that `f = φ ∘ g`. The datum's own condition (d) at `X.pair` identifies
`C^•(g; R)` with `𝒦•(X.pair)` in `D(R)` over the augmentations. Base change along `φ` carries
that identification to one of `C^•(f; A)` with `K(A, I)`: the two comparisons
`C^•(g; R) ⊗^L_R A ⟶ C^•(f; A)` and `𝒦•(X.pair) ⊗^L_R A ⟶ K(A, I)` are isomorphisms, the first
by `Stacks.CechRingBaseChange.isIso_derivedBaseChange_extendedComplexMap` and the second by
`Stacks.PairSite.germBaseChange`, and the augmentations are carried along because condition (a)
holds on the nose for both models
(`Stacks.CechRingBaseChange.extendedComplexMap_augmentation` and
`Stacks.PairSite.germComplexMap_augmentation`). The assembly is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares`.

That the generating family upstairs may be chosen to be a lift of the *prescribed* family `f` is
what makes this reachable: the index category only ever produces *some* generating family, and
condition (d) quantifies over all of them. -/
theorem colimitCechIso (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) : ColimitCechIso Dat := by
  intro A _ r f I hI hf
  obtain ⟨X, g, hg1, hg2, -⟩ := PairOver.exists_pairOver_lift_span f hf
  have hfam : mapFamily X.hom g = f := funext hg1
  subst hfam
  obtain ⟨e₀, he₀⟩ := Dat.exists_cech_iso X.pair g hg2
  have hε : e₀.hom ≫ DerivedCategory.Q.map (sectionsAugmentation Dat.augmentation X.pair) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentation g
        (ModuleCat.of X.pair.ring X.pair.ring)) :=
    LocalCohomology.comp_eq_of_comp_iso_inv _ _
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} X.pair.ring) 0).app
        (ModuleCat.of X.pair.ring X.pair.ring)) _ he₀
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := LocalCohomology.exists_iso_of_augmentation_squares X.hom
    (LocalCohomology.extendedCechComplex g (ModuleCat.of X.pair.ring X.pair.ring))
    (sectionsComplex Dat.complex X.pair)
    (LocalCohomology.extendedCechComplex (mapFamily X.hom g) (ModuleCat.of A A))
    ((colimitComplexFunctor hI).obj Dat.complex)
    (extendedComplexMap X.hom g) (germComplexMap hI Dat.complex X)
    (LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentation g (ModuleCat.of X.pair.ring X.pair.ring))
    (sectionsAugmentation Dat.augmentation X.pair)
    (LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentation (mapFamily X.hom g) (ModuleCat.of A A))
    (colimitAugmentation hI Dat.augmentation)
    (extendedComplexMap_augmentation X.hom g)
    (germComplexMap_augmentation hI Dat.augmentation X)
    (isIso_derivedBaseChange_extendedComplexMap X.hom g) (germBaseChange Dat hI X) e₀ hε
  refine ⟨e, ?_⟩
  have hunfold : LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentationHom (mapFamily X.hom g)
        (ModuleCat.of A A) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (LocalCohomology.extendedCechAugmentation (mapFamily X.hom g)
          (ModuleCat.of A A)) ≫
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctorIsoCompQ (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).app
          (ModuleCat.of A A)).inv := rfl
  rw [hunfold, ← Category.assoc, he]

/-- **Step 2 of [Stacks, Tag 099D] with both of its derived-category conditions discharged**: a
Čech datum on the category of presented pairs gives a functorial Čech datum for *all* pairs
`(A, I)` with `I` finitely generated, with no hypothesis beyond the datum. This is
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_functorialCechData_of_presented` with its two hypotheses supplied by
`Stacks.PairSite.colimitBaseChange` — condition (c) — and `Stacks.PairSite.colimitCechIso` —
condition (d).

No `@[stacks 099D]` attribute is attached: the tag asks for an unconditional
`Nonempty Stacks.LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData`, and this statement still takes a
`Stacks.PairSite.PresentedCechDatum` as input. Feeding it
`Stacks.PairSite.exists_presentedCechDatum` — step 3 — gives that unconditional term, and the
attribute sits there, on `Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_functorialCechData`. -/
theorem exists_functorialCechData (Dat : PresentedCechDatum.{u}) :
    Nonempty LocalCohomology.FunctorialCechData.{u} :=
  exists_functorialCechData_of_presented Dat (colimitBaseChange Dat) (colimitCechIso Dat)

end Stacks.PairSite

end
